1
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,822
Surprise!

2
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:45,243
Happy birthday, Daddy!

3
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:54,753
Make a wish!

4
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,088
I wish...
I'm not going to tell you.

5
00:04:57,339 --> 00:05:00,759
Come on, blow them out!

6
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,097
Give me some sugar, girl.

7
00:05:06,348 --> 00:05:10,852
One more candle and the smoke alarm
would've gone off.

8
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:16,733
The big 5-0.

9
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:20,528
You know, your beard's getting gray.
Kind of makes you look old.

10
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:23,782
It's all right. I still love you.

11
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:26,951
Bye, Pa.

12
00:07:13,475 --> 00:07:16,186
Good morning!

13
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:20,273
- Where's Rianne?
- She's upstairs.

14
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,192
Good morning.

15
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,444
- That's my bacon!
- It's mine now.

16
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,821
Don't you close doors around here?

17
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:30,033
Baby, what's this on my tie?

18
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,868
That is an ugly spot.

19
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:34,371
Thanks. Sharp as a tack.

20
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:37,374
I'm thinking of going on "Jeopardy".

21
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:41,586
Just don't take any questions
about cooking.

22
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,258
Don't step in the egg!

23
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:52,514
What am I thinking? I should have
checked the floor for egg!

24
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:57,894
Do you know a man named
Michael Hunsaker?

25
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:01,439
Jesus! Michael Hunsaker!

26
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,692
- What did he want?
- Your office called.

27
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:06,069
He's tried to reach you
for three days.

28
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:09,698
I haven't talked to him in...

29
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,866
...12 years!

30
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,410
Wait a minute.

31
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,413
That would make me...

32
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:18,415
...50!

33
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:20,959
That means that you're...

34
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,752
We're not gonna discuss it.

35
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:26,214
Forget the eggs.

36
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,677
How come I never heard
of Michael Hunsaker?

37
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:32,637
Just never talked about him.

38
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,431
Vietnam buddy?

39
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:38,226
Eat your own cake. Vietnam buddy.

40
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,353
Nick and the kids
left without me.

41
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:44,024
He left without you? Come on,
I never get enough of my baby.

42
00:08:44,274 --> 00:08:47,944
This is my New Year's Eve dress.
Do you like it? Isn't it cool?

43
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:51,114
It's beautiful.

44
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:54,868
Have a good birthday.

45
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:05,086
Goddamn heartbreaker!

46
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:40,580
{y:i}A lot of people think
{y:i}this is a Superbowl. They're wrong.

47
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:44,250
{y:i}How much would you expect to pay
{y:i}for something like this?

48
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:46,544
{y:i}I'm offering you a Superbowl offer.

49
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:49,297
{y:i}A Superbowl of value
{y:i}on selected items.

50
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:52,592
{y:i}How much would you pay...?

51
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:20,704
I'll buy you a new one.

52
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:16,468
Perfect. Happy fiftieth, Rog.

53
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:22,098
{y:i}Shooting in progress.

54
00:11:22,349 --> 00:11:25,977
{y:i}Three down. Code three.

55
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:31,858
Four-King-32,
en route to the sniper call.

56
00:11:50,877 --> 00:11:54,130
Get down!

57
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:59,260
Look who's here.

58
00:12:04,474 --> 00:12:07,143
- What do you got here?
- Sniper, sir.

59
00:12:07,394 --> 00:12:09,729
Shooting kids, one officer down.

60
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:13,483
He's a nightmare. He's still inside.
We can't get to him.

61
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,860
- You got a SWAT team coming?
- No ETA.

62
00:12:16,111 --> 00:12:18,196
I'll see you around.

63
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:22,075
Let me through! Let me through!

64
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:27,747
Nine years old!

65
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,834
Nine?

66
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:33,003
How good a shot is he?

67
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:36,381
- What do you mean?
- Is he random or specific?

68
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:37,841
He shot at random.

69
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,509
- You make the weapon?
- Automatic.

70
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:43,304
- Hostages or anything like that?
- Not that we know of.

71
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:46,433
Where you going?

72
00:12:46,975 --> 00:12:50,437
Get the hell back here.

73
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:57,277
Get down. You're in the line of fire.
Get down.

74
00:13:02,073 --> 00:13:06,286
Get out of here. He'll shoot you!

75
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:11,291
Hello, Mr. Sniper, sir.

76
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:14,419
Get away!

77
00:13:25,597 --> 00:13:28,725
I'm still here, asshole.

78
00:13:28,767 --> 00:13:31,394
Or do you only do kids?

79
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:34,689
Shut up!

80
00:13:47,786 --> 00:13:51,122
Go on, move, move!

81
00:13:57,212 --> 00:14:01,966
You're one psycho son of a bitch,
but you're good.

82
00:14:36,751 --> 00:14:40,296
Happy birthday, Rog!

83
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,806
We got a hooker.

84
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:53,810
No, it's Dixie. Would you please
tell these bozos to lay off?

85
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,145
You bozos, lay off.

86
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:58,148
Had a jumper here last night.
She saw it happen.

87
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,316
Get her statement, send her home.

88
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:03,695
Thanks. I'm beat.
You know how it is.

89
00:15:03,945 --> 00:15:06,364
All dressed up, no one to blow.

90
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:09,451
You're hilarious!
I can't believe you damn cops!

91
00:15:09,701 --> 00:15:12,912
The jumper's name is Amanda Hunsaker.

92
00:15:13,163 --> 00:15:14,831
Age 22.

93
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:19,044
Prostitute. One arrest,
no convictions. Born in Tennessee.

94
00:15:19,294 --> 00:15:22,047
- Parents...
- What was the name?

95
00:15:22,297 --> 00:15:24,674
The parents.

96
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,427
Michael and Claire.

97
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:29,721
You know them?

98
00:15:29,971 --> 00:15:33,016
Right. Find out who bought it,
who's paying the bills.

99
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:37,395
- That will take some looking into.
- So look!

100
00:16:02,921 --> 00:16:05,256
Hello, honey.

101
00:16:05,507 --> 00:16:08,051
Give me the number
for Michael Hunsaker.

102
00:16:08,301 --> 00:16:10,929
{y:i}The man we talked about?
{y:i}Your Vietnam buddy?

103
00:16:11,179 --> 00:16:14,307
- You just mentioned him this morning.
{y:i}- What's wrong?

104
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:18,395
His daughter just dove out a window.

105
00:16:21,731 --> 00:16:24,526
I got it.

106
00:16:42,377 --> 00:16:45,839
Good, huh? Tasty? Smooth?

107
00:16:47,382 --> 00:16:50,635
- Yeah, that's good.
- You better fucking believe it.

108
00:16:50,885 --> 00:16:52,554
Let's do it. How much?

109
00:16:52,804 --> 00:16:55,015
How much for how much?

110
00:16:55,265 --> 00:16:56,433
For all of it.

111
00:16:56,683 --> 00:16:59,728
You want it all? He wants it all.

112
00:16:59,978 --> 00:17:03,440
- All right!
- Maybe a nice tree to put it under.

113
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:05,150
You want a tree?

114
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,985
I'll tell you what.

115
00:17:07,235 --> 00:17:10,488
I'll give you the best tree
on the lot for nothing.

116
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:13,324
But the shit's gonna cost you...

117
00:17:13,575 --> 00:17:14,784
...a hundred.

118
00:17:15,035 --> 00:17:15,952
That much?

119
00:17:16,202 --> 00:17:19,497
That's a fair price.

120
00:17:20,331 --> 00:17:22,208
You only live once.

121
00:17:22,459 --> 00:17:24,961
Get this together here.

122
00:17:25,211 --> 00:17:26,880
20, 40...

123
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:28,256
...50, 70...

124
00:17:28,506 --> 00:17:32,761
- What the fuck?
- Hey, man!

125
00:17:33,011 --> 00:17:34,554
Shut up, I'm losing count.

126
00:17:34,804 --> 00:17:37,515
93, 94, 95, 96...

127
00:17:37,766 --> 00:17:39,434
Forget it, dumbshit!

128
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:41,519
One hundred thousand!

129
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:45,357
One hundred thousand dollars!

130
00:17:45,607 --> 00:17:47,192
A hundred thousand?

131
00:17:47,442 --> 00:17:52,030
I can't afford that. Not on my salary.
But look, I got a better idea.

132
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:57,577
Let me say I take the whole stash
off your hands for free...

133
00:17:57,827 --> 00:18:02,332
...and you assholes go to jail.
What do you say?

134
00:18:02,624 --> 00:18:08,338
I could read you your rights, but you
already know what your rights are.

135
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,258
This badge ain't real.

136
00:18:12,509 --> 00:18:13,593
You ain't real.

137
00:18:13,843 --> 00:18:17,806
You sure are a crazy son of a bitch.

138
00:18:18,682 --> 00:18:20,517
I'm crazy?

139
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:22,769
You think I am crazy?

140
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:26,189
I'll show you...

141
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:32,320
That's a real badge, I'm a real cop
and this is a real gun.

142
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,655
Okay, pal.

143
00:18:33,905 --> 00:18:37,075
Noses in the dirt, assholes!

144
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:50,714
Where's your buddy?

145
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:54,259
What do you got?

146
00:18:54,509 --> 00:18:57,804
Three down and one loose.
He's got a red shirt.

147
00:18:58,054 --> 00:19:01,016
Okay, let's go.

148
00:19:01,516 --> 00:19:05,103
Freeze! Give me the gun! Up, up!

149
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:07,397
How's it feel, sucker?

150
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:08,606
Shoot him!

151
00:19:08,857 --> 00:19:09,816
Drop it!

152
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:11,818
Shoot him! Shoot him!

153
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:15,447
- Shut the fuck up!
- Shoot this prick!

154
00:19:15,697 --> 00:19:18,283
Shoot him! Somebody
shoot this prick!

155
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:19,951
Shoot me.

156
00:19:20,201 --> 00:19:22,579
Shut up! Put them down!

157
00:19:22,829 --> 00:19:25,874
- I warn you! I'm going to shoot you!
- Shoot him!

158
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:27,917
Shut the fuck up! Shut up!

159
00:19:28,168 --> 00:19:31,838
Shoot me! Shoot him!

160
00:19:37,844 --> 00:19:40,472
Get him out of there.

161
00:19:40,722 --> 00:19:43,767
It ain't worth it.

162
00:20:02,869 --> 00:20:05,163
Come on, Sam. Thattaboy.

163
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:08,583
Hey, guys.

164
00:20:09,501 --> 00:20:13,588
Up you go, Sam. Come on.

165
00:20:15,006 --> 00:20:17,175
How you been there, Sam?

166
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:19,052
Been catching mice today?

167
00:20:19,302 --> 00:20:20,970
What kind of a day did you have?

168
00:20:21,221 --> 00:20:23,973
You haven't been doing anything,
lazy son of a bitch.

169
00:20:24,224 --> 00:20:29,437
I'll get you a sandwich,
because that's all there is.

170
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:32,607
Beer for me.

171
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:36,820
Looks like turkey.
I got us a surprise.

172
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:42,492
Thirteen-inch color TV set.
We can watch reruns of "Lassie".

173
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:45,745
Hey, wait up already!

174
00:23:11,474 --> 00:23:14,686
{y:i}Merry Christmas!

175
00:23:41,421 --> 00:23:44,758
I miss you...

176
00:23:45,884 --> 00:23:49,095
...Victoria Lynn.

177
00:24:01,524 --> 00:24:05,070
That's silly, isn't it?

178
00:24:09,324 --> 00:24:12,660
I'll see you later.

179
00:24:12,952 --> 00:24:16,414
I'll see you much later.

180
00:24:21,044 --> 00:24:24,422
Once more with feeling on three.

181
00:24:24,673 --> 00:24:30,220
Damn it, Cooley. Do it on three,
or go on the street.

182
00:24:33,306 --> 00:24:36,643
{y:i}Silent night

183
00:24:36,893 --> 00:24:39,604
Are you telling me
Riggs is playing a game?

184
00:24:39,854 --> 00:24:43,274
Sure. He wants the cash.
But he'll come around.

185
00:24:43,525 --> 00:24:45,777
That's a very dangerous
attitude to take.

186
00:24:46,027 --> 00:24:50,824
Remember, his wife of 11 years
was just killed in a car accident.

187
00:24:51,074 --> 00:24:54,869
- He pulls his gun when he shouldn't.
- I know all about him.

188
00:24:55,120 --> 00:24:56,287
He's a tough bastard.

189
00:24:56,538 --> 00:24:59,749
He's on the edge. I'm telling you,
he may be psychotic.

190
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,918
That's a bunch of psych bullshit.

191
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:05,130
You're making a mistake
by keeping him in the field.

192
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:07,048
The man is suicidal.

193
00:25:07,298 --> 00:25:10,135
You're sure of that diagnosis?
You have no doubts?

194
00:25:10,385 --> 00:25:12,053
There are no absolutes in life.

195
00:25:12,303 --> 00:25:14,973
End of discussion.
We're going to wait.

196
00:25:15,223 --> 00:25:17,809
If he offs himself,
then we'll know I was wrong.

197
00:25:18,059 --> 00:25:22,939
You're making a mistake,
because if you're wrong...

198
00:25:28,570 --> 00:25:30,530
Asshole!

199
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:33,408
Roger, you're
way behind the times.

200
00:25:33,658 --> 00:25:37,704
The guys in the '80s aren't tough.
They're sensitive people.

201
00:25:37,954 --> 00:25:42,500
They show emotions around women,
shit like that.

202
00:25:42,709 --> 00:25:44,252
I think I'm an '80s man.

203
00:25:44,502 --> 00:25:46,004
How do you figure?

204
00:25:46,254 --> 00:25:47,839
Last night...

205
00:25:48,089 --> 00:25:51,634
...I cried in bed. How's that?

206
00:25:53,136 --> 00:25:55,013
Were you with a woman?

207
00:25:55,263 --> 00:25:58,725
I was alone. Why do you think
I was crying? Merry Christmas.

208
00:25:58,975 --> 00:26:01,686
Sounds like an '80s man to me.

209
00:26:01,936 --> 00:26:04,272
- News on the Hunsaker case.
- That was quick.

210
00:26:04,522 --> 00:26:08,318
So was the autopsy.
They're not calling it a suicide.

211
00:26:08,568 --> 00:26:12,947
Surprise, surprise. The coroner
found evidence she used barbiturates.

212
00:26:13,198 --> 00:26:14,657
Brilliant detective work.

213
00:26:14,908 --> 00:26:16,659
There were pills all over.

214
00:26:16,910 --> 00:26:19,329
Right. That's not the surprise.

215
00:26:19,579 --> 00:26:22,374
The surprise is
the pills were doctored.

216
00:26:22,624 --> 00:26:25,085
The capsules were loaded
with drain cleaner.

217
00:26:25,335 --> 00:26:26,503
She'd have died anyway.

218
00:26:26,753 --> 00:26:27,754
This case stinks.

219
00:26:28,004 --> 00:26:32,133
You know,
you looked younger with the beard.

220
00:26:32,384 --> 00:26:35,303
Thanks, captain.

221
00:26:35,595 --> 00:26:36,888
You shaved the beard.

222
00:26:37,138 --> 00:26:38,682
Some detective.

223
00:26:38,932 --> 00:26:40,892
Two more things.

224
00:26:41,142 --> 00:26:43,687
The condition
of the sheets indicates...

225
00:26:43,937 --> 00:26:46,898
...someone else was
in bed with Amanda. That's "A".

226
00:26:47,148 --> 00:26:48,191
What's "B"?

227
00:26:48,441 --> 00:26:51,820
"B" is, you're breaking in
a new partner on this.

228
00:26:52,070 --> 00:26:53,071
Partner again?

229
00:26:53,321 --> 00:26:56,866
Some cat on loan from Dope.
Real burnout, on the edge.

230
00:26:57,117 --> 00:26:59,703
Perfect.

231
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:03,289
Gun!

232
00:27:08,670 --> 00:27:11,923
Rog, meet your new partner.

233
00:27:14,175 --> 00:27:18,388
I'm too old for this shit.

234
00:27:21,141 --> 00:27:23,601
There are those who
say you're a good cop.

235
00:27:23,852 --> 00:27:25,687
I try.

236
00:27:25,937 --> 00:27:31,484
I heard about the little
stunt yesterday. Pretty heroic.

237
00:27:32,193 --> 00:27:33,945
I pulled your file.

238
00:27:34,195 --> 00:27:37,907
Said you worked in the Phoenix
project in Vietnam. That right?

239
00:27:38,158 --> 00:27:41,369
Assassination stuff.
It's over, you know.

240
00:27:41,619 --> 00:27:43,371
What is?

241
00:27:43,621 --> 00:27:44,622
The war.

242
00:27:44,873 --> 00:27:46,541
Yes, I know.

243
00:27:46,791 --> 00:27:50,003
Just thought I'd remind you.

244
00:27:50,587 --> 00:27:54,132
That's some serious shit you carry.

245
00:27:54,382 --> 00:27:57,594
Be my guest.

246
00:28:00,889 --> 00:28:04,726
9mm Beretta. Takes 15 in the mag,
one up the pipe...

247
00:28:04,976 --> 00:28:08,730
...wide ejection port, no feed jams.

248
00:28:08,980 --> 00:28:10,065
What have you got?

249
00:28:10,315 --> 00:28:12,984
Four-inch Smith.

250
00:28:12,984 --> 00:28:15,612
Six-shooter?

251
00:28:15,653 --> 00:28:18,782
A lot of old-timers carry those.

252
00:28:21,618 --> 00:28:24,245
File also said you're heavy
into martial arts.

253
00:28:24,496 --> 00:28:27,957
Tai chi and all that killer stuff.

254
00:28:28,208 --> 00:28:32,087
I suppose we have to register you
as a lethal weapon.

255
00:28:32,337 --> 00:28:36,174
Let's just cut the shit.
We both know why I was transferred.

256
00:28:36,424 --> 00:28:40,762
Everybody thinks I'm suicidal,
so nobody wants to work with me.

257
00:28:41,012 --> 00:28:43,473
Some think I'm faking
to draw psycho pension...

258
00:28:43,723 --> 00:28:47,644
...so nobody wants to work with me.
