- Pleased to meet you.

558
00:50:25,525 --> 00:50:27,652
Martin's going to join us for dinner.

559
00:50:27,902 --> 00:50:30,989
- Roast okay with you?
- What's for dinner?

560
00:50:31,239 --> 00:50:34,159
We'll see what's for dinner.

561
00:50:34,409 --> 00:50:37,495
This is a brown, sticky...

562
00:50:37,746 --> 00:50:39,164
It's roast.

563
00:50:39,414 --> 00:50:41,791
How about a brown
roast-like substance?

564
00:50:42,042 --> 00:50:45,003
- Roger, you're being an asshole.
- I try not to be.

565
00:50:45,253 --> 00:50:46,963
- Want a drink?
- What do you got?

566
00:50:47,213 --> 00:50:49,883
We have Canadian Mist...

567
00:50:50,133 --> 00:50:55,263
- You like Canadian Mist?
- Honey, it's in the back.

568
00:50:55,930 --> 00:50:59,351
How come we didn't have fish?
I thought we had fish tonight.

569
00:50:59,601 --> 00:51:01,186
Don't worry about the fish.

570
00:51:01,436 --> 00:51:03,480
Getting defensive...
Ever go fishing?

571
00:51:03,730 --> 00:51:08,234
Not since I was a kid.
I used to go spearfishing.

572
00:51:08,610 --> 00:51:11,529
All I caught was a cold.

573
00:51:12,447 --> 00:51:14,157
I got that boat out there.

574
00:51:14,407 --> 00:51:16,534
Rianne, get the dessert.

575
00:51:16,785 --> 00:51:19,954
Rianne! Your mother said
get the dessert.

576
00:51:20,205 --> 00:51:23,375
- Get the dessert. Get to it!
- Shut up.

577
00:51:23,625 --> 00:51:28,254
Catalina Island. Nothing exciting,
but I catch my allotment.

578
00:51:28,505 --> 00:51:34,427
You can catch a few things out there.
I caught my wife out there.

579
00:51:34,427 --> 00:51:36,096
Nice fishing out there.

580
00:51:36,346 --> 00:51:38,098
Mr. Riggs, care for a tart?

581
00:51:38,348 --> 00:51:41,559
Thank you, yes. Call me Martin.

582
00:51:41,851 --> 00:51:43,603
Mr. Riggs.

583
00:51:43,853 --> 00:51:46,147
Sit down.

584
00:51:46,398 --> 00:51:50,652
Rianne, it's not the first time
we've had company.

585
00:51:54,823 --> 00:51:58,743
{y:i}My name is Carrie, I'm no fairy
{y:i}My sister's cherry

586
00:51:58,993 --> 00:52:02,455
{y:i}She's in love with a guy
{y:i}named Martin...

587
00:52:02,706 --> 00:52:03,665
Nicholas!

588
00:52:03,915 --> 00:52:06,626
Come on. It was really good!

589
00:52:06,876 --> 00:52:09,462
Yeah, Dad! Why don't you try it?

590
00:52:09,713 --> 00:52:12,173
It was good.

591
00:52:13,216 --> 00:52:14,759
Yeah, there you go.

592
00:52:15,010 --> 00:52:17,595
{y:i}I'm gonna find a partner
{y:i}My name is Roger

593
00:52:17,846 --> 00:52:21,975
{y:i}And I need to be modger
{y:i}And a secret hodger

594
00:52:22,225 --> 00:52:23,685
You need some help.

595
00:52:23,935 --> 00:52:26,896
I am awful!

596
00:52:39,534 --> 00:52:43,621
Hey, sarge! Thanks for
taking out the garbage.

597
00:52:43,872 --> 00:52:48,251
But, honey,
I'm entertaining our guest.

598
00:52:50,337 --> 00:52:52,172
What do you think?

599
00:52:52,422 --> 00:52:55,175
It's nice. You know
anything about boats?

600
00:52:55,425 --> 00:52:58,386
- I know what they cost.
- Can you sail this?

601
00:52:58,636 --> 00:53:01,848
What's wrong with you?
It's not a sailboat.

602
00:53:02,098 --> 00:53:03,475
That's what I thought.

603
00:53:03,725 --> 00:53:08,605
There's no trick. That's the front,
that's the back, water all around.

604
00:53:08,855 --> 00:53:13,068
Why you gotta make things
so complicated?

605
00:53:15,570 --> 00:53:19,532
I don't. Things get complicated
all by themselves.

606
00:53:19,783 --> 00:53:22,077
You mean Amanda Hunsaker's
murder, huh?

607
00:53:22,327 --> 00:53:25,163
Did I mention that? I didn't.

608
00:53:25,413 --> 00:53:28,958
Didn't have to.
I can read your mind.

609
00:53:29,292 --> 00:53:31,836
What's the matter with you?

610
00:53:32,087 --> 00:53:34,297
- Why is there a problem?
- There's no problem.

611
00:53:34,547 --> 00:53:36,758
You got one dead girl
and one dead guy.

612
00:53:37,008 --> 00:53:41,596
The guy kills the girl. We kill him
because he wants us to be dead guys.

613
00:53:41,846 --> 00:53:44,683
That's easy for you to say.

614
00:53:44,933 --> 00:53:46,810
A sugar daddy is dealing drugs.

615
00:53:47,060 --> 00:53:50,563
She said, did or saw something
she wasn't supposed to.

616
00:53:50,814 --> 00:53:54,943
He pitches her off the balcony
into the sweet by-and-by.

617
00:53:55,193 --> 00:53:57,445
That's why he came at us
with a shotgun today.

618
00:53:57,696 --> 00:54:01,866
I'm sorry. It's just a little
too neat. I can't swallow it.

619
00:54:02,117 --> 00:54:07,205
Of course it's neat.
What's wrong with neat? I like neat.

620
00:54:07,455 --> 00:54:11,376
By neat, you mean simple.

621
00:54:12,460 --> 00:54:14,546
- You okay?
- Watch out!

622
00:54:14,796 --> 00:54:17,215
What button did you push?

623
00:54:17,465 --> 00:54:20,385
Where's my manual?

624
00:54:20,635 --> 00:54:22,929
Is this what you're
looking for, captain?

625
00:54:23,179 --> 00:54:25,056
You asshole!

626
00:54:25,306 --> 00:54:29,728
Didn't mean to interrupt one of those
